It is a quiet Tuesday evening in my apartment.
I clear my small kitchen table.
The plates are washed, and the table is wiped down.
I enjoy the quiet after a long day at the office.
But suddenly I remember an important task.
I need to update my contact details on my electricity provider's website.
I have received an email with a reminder from them.
In the message it says: "Your details must be updated before Wednesday."
That is already tomorrow!
It is a really boring digital chore.
I usually put off that kind of thing until the last minute.
Actually, it often gets completely forgotten until I get a warning.
But tonight I want to be ahead of things.
I sit down on a chair and look at the empty table.
My computer is in my work bag out in the hallway.
I do not have the energy to fetch and start it now.
Fortunately, I usually just use my phone for the small tasks.
I take the phone out of my pocket with a heavy sigh.
Now it just needs to be over and done with.
